"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Fashion trends\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Fashion trends refer to the prevailing styles and preferences in clothing and accessories that change over time, influenced by various social, cultural, economic, and technological factors. They reflect the values, beliefs, and attitudes of different eras and have been a significant form of self-expression, cultural identity, and social commentary throughout history.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Role in Society\": \"Reflecting values, beliefs, and attitudes of different eras\",\n        \"Historical Evolution\": \"From ancient civilizations to the modern era, fashion trends have evolved continuously, influenced by culture, technology, politics, and economics\",\n        \"Influence on Self-Expression\": \"Fashion has been a powerful form of self-expression and cultural identity\",\n        \"Impact of Economic Conditions\": \"Economic conditions, such as the Great Depression, can lead to more conservative and practical fashion designs\",\n        \"Impact of Social Movements\": \"Social, cultural, and political movements can drive rapid changes in fashion trends\",\n        \"Influence of Media\": \"Social media platforms and fashion magazines have revolutionized the way people discover and engage with fashion\",\n        \"Influence of Technology\": \"Mass production techniques and the printing press have made fashion more accessible and widespread\",\n        \"Influence of Individualism\": \"The turn of the millennium brought about a more eclectic and individualistic approach to fashion\",\n        \"Impact of Sustainability\": \"Sustainable fashion practices, such as upcycling, recycling, and ethical sourcing, have gained traction in the 21st century\",\n        \"Impact of Prosperity\": \"Post-World War II prosperity led to a resurgence of glamour and luxury in fashion\",\n        \"Impact of War\": \"World War II influenced fashion trends, leading to more practical and functional clothing\",\n        \"Impact of Religion\": \"During the Middle Ages, fashion trends were heavily influenced by religion and social hierarchy\",\n        \"Impact of Social Hierarchy\": \"Sumptuary laws regulated what different classes of society could wear, reflecting the influence of social hierarchy on fashion\",\n        \"Impact of Art and Culture\": \"The Renaissance period saw a resurgence of interest in art, culture, and fashion, leading to more elaborate and artistic designs\",\n        \"Impact of Youth Culture\": \"Youth culture in the 1960s and 1970s influenced fashion trends, characterized by rebellion and experimentation\",\n        \"Impact of Iconic Figures\": \"Iconic figures like Audrey Hepburn and Marilyn Monroe popularized specific styles in the 1950s\",\n        \"Impact of Supermodels\": \"Supermodels like Cindy Crawford and Naomi Campbell helped popularize designer brands and high-end fashion labels\",\n        \"Impact of Ready-to-Wear\": \"Mass production techniques allowed for the creation of ready-to-wear clothing, making fashion more accessible to the general population\",\n        \"Impact of Department Stores\": \"The rise of department stores further democratized fashion, allowing people to follow and purchase the latest trends at affordable prices\",\n        \"Impact of Economic Hardship\": \"The Great Depression led to a more conservative and practical approach to fashion\",\n        \"Impact of Excess and Opulence\": \"The 1980s and 1990s were marked by bold colors, exaggerated silhouettes, and flashy accessories\",\n        \"Impact of Cultural Shifts\": \"The Roaring Twenties marked a shift towards more relaxed and liberating clothing styles for women\",\n        \"Impact of Industrial Revolution\": \"The Industrial Revolution brought significant changes to the fashion industry, including mass production and new materials\",\n        \"Impact of Renaissance\": \"The Renaissance period saw a resurgence of interest in art, culture, and fashion, influencing the design and materials of clothing\",\n        \"Impact of Modern Era\": \"In the 21st century, fashion trends have become more diverse and inclusive, with a greater emphasis on sustainability, diversity, and body positivity\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"society\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Construct\",\n      \"description\": \"Society refers to a group of individuals involved in persistent social interaction, or a large social group sharing the same geographical or social territory, typically subject to the same political authority and dominant cultural expectations. In the context of fashion, society\\\"s values, beliefs, and attitudes are reflected through fashion trends and practices.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Values\": \"Diversity, inclusivity, sustainability, and body positivity\",\n        \"Era\": \"21st century\",\n        \"Approach to Fashion\": \"More eclectic and individualistic\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"royalty\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Class\",\n      \"description\": \"Royalty refers to the highest social class in a monarchy, typically consisting of the monarch and their immediate family members. They often wear luxurious and distinctive clothing as a symbol of their status and identity.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Status\": \"Highest social class in a monarchy\",\n        \"Identity\": \"Monarch and immediate family members\",\n        \"Clothing Material\": \"Expensive fabrics like silk and velvet\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"20th century\",\n      \"type\": \"Time Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The 20th century spans from 1901 to 2000 and is marked by significant social, cultural, and political changes, including rapid changes in fashion trends.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Start Year\": \"1901\",\n        \"End Year\": \"2000\",\n        \"Characteristics\": \"Rapid changes in fashion trends, driven by social, cultural, and political movements\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"The Roaring Twenties\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The Roaring Twenties was a decade of significant social, economic, and cultural change, particularly noted for its shift towards more relaxed and liberating clothing styles, especially among women.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Time Period\": \"1920s\",\n        \"Fashion Trend\": \"More relaxed and liberating clothing styles, shorter hemlines, loose-fitting silhouettes, and boyish cuts for women\",\n        \"Social Impact\": \"Marked a period of social liberation and change, particularly in women\\\"s fashion and lifestyle\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"designer brands\",\n      \"type\": \"Fashion Brand\",\n      \"description\": \"Designer brands are high-end fashion labels known for their unique designs, quality, and often luxurious materials. They have played a significant role in the fashion industry, especially in the modern era, by being associated with supermodels and the wealthy elite.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Era of Influence\": \"Modern Era, 1980s and 1990s\",\n        \"Characteristics\": \"Unique designs, high quality, luxurious materials\",\n        \"Target Audience\": \"Wealthy elite, fashion-conscious individuals\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Renaissance\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The Renaissance was a period of European history, from the 14th to the 17th century, regarded as the cultural bridge between the Middle Ages and modern history. It was characterized by a resurgence of interest in art, culture, and fashion.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Middle Ages\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The Middle Ages, or Medieval period, lasted from the 5th to the 15th century. It was a time when fashion trends were heavily influenced by religion and social hierarchy.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Industrial Revolution\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Event\",\n      \"description\": \"The Industrial Revolution was a period from about 1760 to sometime between 1820 and 1840. It marked a major turning point in history, affecting almost every aspect of daily life, including the fashion industry.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Great Depression\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Event\",\n      \"description\": \"The Great Depression was a severe worldwide economic depression that took place during the 1930s. It had a profound impact on various aspects of life, including fashion.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"1960s and 1970s\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The 1960s and 1970s were decades characterized by significant social, cultural, and political changes, including a spirit of rebellion and experimentation.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"1950s\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The 1950s were a decade marked by post-World War II prosperity and the rise of iconic fashion figures.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"1980s and 1990s\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The 1980s and 1990s were decades characterized by excess and opulence, with bold and flashy fashion trends.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Roaring Twenties\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The Roaring Twenties, also known as the Jazz Age, was a decade of economic prosperity and cultural change, particularly in the United States.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"21st Century\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The 21st century is characterized by rapid technological advancements, globalization, and a growing awareness of environmental and social issues.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Social Media\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"Social media platforms like Instagram and TikTok are digital tools that allow users to share and consume content, including fashion-related posts and videos.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Printing Press\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"The printing press is a device for applying pressure to an inked surface resting upon a print medium, thereby transferring the ink. It was invented in the 15th century and had a profound impact on the dissemination of information.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mass Production\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"Mass production is the production of large amounts of standardized products, often using assembly lines. It became prominent during the Industrial Revolution.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Department Stores\",\n      \"type\": \"Retail\",\n      \"description\": \"Department stores are large retail establishments offering a wide range of goods, including clothing and accessories.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Fashion Magazines\",\n      \"type\": \"Media\",\n      \"description\": \"Fashion magazines are publications that focus on fashion, beauty, and lifestyle, often featuring the latest trends and fashion advice.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Sustainable Fashion Practices\",\n      \"type\": \"Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"Sustainable fashion practices include upcycling, recycling, and ethical sourcing, aimed at reducing the environmental impact of the fashion industry.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"C