ores are large retail establishments offering a wide range of goods organized into separate departments.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fashion magazines\",\n      \"type\": \"Media\",\n      \"description\": \"Fashion magazines are publications that focus on fashion, beauty, and lifestyle content, often featuring the latest trends and designer profiles.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"sustainable fashion practices\",\n      \"type\": \"Environmental Practice\",\n      \"description\": \"Sustainable fashion practices include methods such as upcycling, recycling, and ethical sourcing to reduce the environmental impact of the fashion industry.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"wealthy elite in Europe\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Group\",\n      \"description\": \"The wealthy elite in Europe are a social group characterized by significant economic resources and influence.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"expensive fabrics\",\n      \"type\": \"Material\",\n      \"description\": \"Expensive fabrics are high-quality materials used in the production of garments, often associated with luxury and high social status.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"status and identity\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Status and identity are social and personal attributes that define an individual\\\"s position and role within a community or society.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Rapid Changes in Fashion Trends\",\n      \"type\": \"Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"Fashion trends changed quickly during the 20th century, influenced by various social, cultural, and political movements.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Social Movements\",\n      \"type\": \"Factor\",\n      \"description\": \"Social movements, such as civil rights and feminism, playe